         "label": "PL - FAQ",
         "name": "module_9",
         "params": {
          "items": [
           {
            "answer": "<p>We use minimal preservatives where required to maintain microbial safety, and avoid them entirely where the formulation allows (high-acid, high-alcohol, or low-water-activity products). Preservative system is chosen based on the specific formulation, shelf life requirements, and brand positioning.</p>",
            "question": "Do you use preservatives?"
           },
           {
            "answer": "<p>Most liquid formulations have a 12 to 24-month shelf life depending on actives, preservative system, and packaging. Liquid actives generally have shorter intrinsic stability than dry formats. Stability testing for longer claims available on request.</p>",
            "question": "What is the shelf life of a liquid product?"
           },
           {
            "answer": "<p>Yes. Alcohol is sometimes used as a preservative or extraction solvent for herbal liquids, but alcohol-free formulations using vegetable glycerin or other natural carriers are available for kids' products, religious-compliance positioning, or alcohol-sensitive audiences.</p>",
            "question": "Do you offer alcohol-free liquid formulations?"
           },
           {
            "answer": "<p>Yes. Liposomal liquids deliver fat-soluble vitamins and certain compounds with much higher bioavailability than standard formats. This is a premium-priced format, typically used for vitamin C, glutathione, DHEA, curcumin, and similar actives.</p>",
            "question": "Can you do liposomal liquid formulations?"
           },
           {
            "answer": "<p>Both available. Glass is preferred for premium positioning, photosensitive ingredients, and oil-based liquids. Food-grade plastic (PET, HDPE) is preferred for travel-friendly, shatter-resistant, and lower-cost products. Choice depends on positioning and shipping considerations.</p>",
            "question": "Glass or plastic bottles?"
           }
          ],
